  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Issue: \n\nIf an Avatar is bigger than the maximum file size you have set in the Settings it will not be downloaded. The problem is that when you decide to show it, just to see how bad it actually is, and then set the Avatar Display to use the Safety Settings again it will still be downloaded and shown.\n\n**Reproduction Steps:** \n\n1. Find a Users whose Avatar is blocked due to file size\n\n2. Show that Users Avatar Manually \n\n3. Set the Avatar Display Settings back to use Safety Settings\n\nIf you do this you will notice that the Avatar will still be fully downloaded and shown.\n\n# Expected Behavior:\n\nWhen you set the Avatar Display back to use the Safety Settings before the download is complete the download of the Avatar should be aborted. If an Avatar has already finished downloading it should instead just be hidden and removed from the download cache (if possible).\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/gyrf38.mp4",
